  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thirteenth replenishment of IFAD&apos;s resources for the period 2025-2027 (IFAD13) (core and DSF contribution)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Fund for Agricultural Development (IFAD) is an international financial institution and a specialized agency of the United Nations dedicated to eradicating poverty and hunger in rural areas of developing countries. 

This activity appraisal document concerns the Dutch contribution to the thirteenth replenishment of IFAD-13 of USD 92,107,000 and Debt Sustainability Framework contribution of USD 7,893,000 to IFAD-13 for the period 2025-2027. The total contribution is USD 100 million. 

With this core contribution to IFAD-13 the Netherlands aims to contribute to food security worldwide. The goals of IFAD closely align with the Dutch development cooperation policy goals according to the BHOS-nota and the focus areas.</narrative>
  </description>
